{# ============================================================================
   THE WEEK — THE PLANNING SHEET. The design's modules/roster/week.html,
   ported; the same markup renders on variants-pattern/c.html.

   RULED 20–21 sep, graduated from three rounds of options:

     layout C   the fill row inline above the sheet       variants-pattern/
     window C   the calendar tab's nav, 1 / 2 / 4 weeks   variants-pattern/
     cells  A   the calendar tab's own bar                variants-cells/
     folds      a station band folds, the grants idiom    ruled 21 sep

   Owner: "look at how clean the calendar is, as inspiration", and "each
   station section in the sheet as an accordion ... so a user doesn't have to
   scroll for ages", and "contents of The sheet should scroll inside the
   sheet, so the headers stay fixed while the inner content scrolls", and
   "this entire thing needs to be in the sheet header — I didn't even see it
   exists".

   SIX MARKS CAME OFF EVERY CELL BEFORE ANYTHING WAS ADDED: the border, the
   centred text, the radius, the weekend stripes, the dashed box on every off
   day, and the outline on every cell in today's column. What is left is the
   calendar's own bar, and THE ONLY OUTLINED THING ON THE SHEET IS A GAP.

   THE BANDED CARD IS DELIBERATE HERE and is the one on any tab. A tab wears
   the house card; the sheet's head has to carry eight controls on one
   baseline, which is the banded head's whole job.

   COVERAGE MANIFEST — every element of the drawn page, and what it
   MEASURES against the design. Both sides rendered at 1440 in Chrome
   153 (the owner's own binary), read two frames after any scroll:

     design  /areas/kilimani/modules/roster/week.html, served over http
     app     this template, rendered and served flat with shell.css,
             widget.css and this bundle's roster.css

   | element                                 | type    | source                          | interaction                       | design → app                          | status |
   |-----------------------------------------|---------|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------|---------------------------------------|--------|
   | .factband four figures + door           | data    | the sheet's own cells           | door to Roster settings           | 1132×58.3 → 1132×58.3                 | pass   |
   | .factband keys, in order                | chrome  | static                          | none                              | Rangers · Days planned · Short cover · Edited by hand, both | pass |
   | .pgact "Plan the day", then Configure   | control | the day, the frame              | to the plan; to Configure         | 2 actions → 2 (Configure is the frame's) | pass |
   | .prow kicker "Fill from a pattern"      | chrome  | static                          | none                              | 1132×56 → 1132×56                     | pass   |
   | .prow station select                    | control | stations on the books           | which station a fill points at    | present both                          | pass   |
   | .prow .pstrip.lg cycle strip            | data    | the chosen pattern's cycle      | none — redrawn with the select    | present both                          | pass   |
   | .prow pattern select                    | control | the area's patterns             | which cycle fills it              | present both                          | pass   |
   | .prow "from" + start-date select        | control | six mondays around the window   | where the ring starts             | present both                          | pass   |
   | .prow Preview · Fill these days         | control | —                               | says what a fill would do; fills  | present both                          | pass   |
   | .prow2 what it would do, in words       | data    | the last preview, or the rules  | none                              | present both                          | pass   |
   | .prow2 .pfills read-only caption        | data    | the four filling rules          | one door: Watches →               | present both                          | pass   |
   | .sheetcard bounded card                 | chrome  | measured (--sheetmax)           | none                              | 1132×670 → 1132×670                   | pass   |
   | .sheetcard .tab "The sheet"             | chrome  | static                          | none                              | present both                          | pass   |
   | .shead .rb-ttl "N rangers across N"     | data    | the sheet                       | none                              | 1130×56 head, both                    | pass   |
   | .shead eight .mchip on one baseline     | control | the window, stations, weeks     | moves, narrows and resizes it     | 8 chips × 28px high → 8 × 28px        | pass   |
   | .psheetwrap bounded scroller            | chrome  | measured (--sheetmax)           | scrolls, head and days pinned     | head pinned at 0 in both              | pass   |
   | thead th, today tinted                  | data    | the window                      | none                              | 60.3×33 → 60.1×33                     | pass   |
   | thead th.who — the ranger column        | chrome  | static                          | none                              | 257.3 → 258 wide                      | pass   |
   | tr.stfold band head                     | control | a station's rows                | folds that band, per person       | 1100×44 → 1100×44                     | pass   |
   | .stfoldb .stline chevron + name         | chrome  | the station                     | folds the band                    | present both                          | pass   |
   | .stfoldb .stmeta code · size · short    | data    | the postings, and the cover     | none                              | "ST-01 · 5 rangers · 1 short this window" shape, both | pass |
   | td.sepd .cvr — cover, one per day       | data    | duties vs StationWatch.needs    | none                              | 14 per band → 14; token 30×16 → 30×16 | pass   |
   | tr.strow ranger row                     | data    | the postings, in seat order     | none                              | 1100×57 → 1100×57                     | pass   |
   | td.who name + call sign, ONE line       | data    | the posting                     | none                              | one line both; see residual A         | pass   |
   | .cl.bar day cell + dot + mono label     | data    | the duty, coloured by the shift | opens the by-hand menu            | 54.3×52 → 54.1×52; dot 5×5 → 5×5      | pass   |
   | .cl.bar tint reads the stored slot      | data    | Shift.colour via [data-cat]     | none                              | cat tint resolved on both             | pass   |
   | .cl.off                                 | state   | no watch on that day            | opens the by-hand menu            | nothing drawn, both                   | pass   |
   | .cl > .hm corner mark                   | state   | a hand mark on that ranger's day| none                              | present both                          | pass   |
   | .pmenu.dm header, one line of facts     | data    | the cell: who, day, shift, hue  | none                              | present both                          | pass   |
   | .dmr Change the shift                   | control | the area's shifts, as chips     | inline step, then the write       | verb 1 of 5, both                     | pass   |
   | .dmr Move to someone else               | control | the station's other rangers     | inline step, then the write       | verb 2 of 5, both                     | pass   |
   | .dmr Swap with another                  | control | the station's other rangers     | inline step, then the offer       | verb 3 of 5, both                     | pass   |
   | .dmr Give the day off                   | control | the cell's duty                 | one write: off, and a hand mark   | verb 4 of 5, both                     | pass   |
   | .dmr Clear the hand mark                | control | the hand mark on that day       | one write                         | verb 5 of 5, both                     | pass   |
   | .pmenulayer, anchored to the cell       | chrome  | the open cell's anchor-name     | follows it, closes off the band   | see residual C                        | pass   |
   | .pkey under the sheet                   | data    | the area's shifts               | none                              | 1100×23 → 1100×23                     | pass   |
   | .pkey line, without "unfilled"          | data    | the sheet's own figures         | none                              | shift names · off · edited · short station-days · edited · rangers · window | pass |
   | empty sheet                             | state   | an area with no station         | none                              | app only — the design draws no empty  | n/a    |
   | h2.zone "The swap in progress"          | chrome  | static                          | none                              | present both                          | pass   |
   | Swap a watch card                       | control | the trade being put together    | sends the offer                   | present both                          | pass   |
   | Swaps register, latest five             | data    | the window's offers             | none                              | present both                          | pass   |

   RESIDUALS, named rather than quietly carried:

     A  td.who measures 172×23 on the design and 258×57 here. The design's
        global sheet carries an unrelated `.who { display: flex }` (a person
        line in widgets.css) which takes the cell out of the table: the name
        is then clipped at 172 inside a 258 column, with 86px of the column
        empty beside it. This module owns no `.who` outside the sheet, so the
        cell is an ordinary table cell here and the name uses the whole
        column — the design's own words, "name and call sign on ONE line",
        with the clipping artefact left behind.
     B  .cl.bar is 52px tall on both, but on the design that height arrives
        from `.bar` in the same global sheet — a legacy sticky top bar the
        cell collides with by name. The NUMBER is the ruling; it is declared
        here, scoped to `.cl.bar`, rather than inherited from a class this
        module does not own.
     C  the menu's "one-frame 10px slip" was measured and is not one. In
        real Chrome 153 the cell-to-panel gap is 0px drift across every
        frame of a scroll, at two weeks and at four; the 10px was the gauge
        sampling the panel in the same task as the click, before Chrome had
        applied the anchor position for a panel that had just appeared.
        `popover="manual"` in the top layer was tried and measures exactly
        the same — 10px without settling frames, 0px with them — so it is
        not kept: it would be a behaviour change bought for nothing.

   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/base.html.twig' %}

{# WHETHER THIS PERSON MAY PLAN. The door names the pair every write on
   this sheet carries — filling it, offering a watch, publishing the day —
   so a control is drawn only where the route behind it would accept it. #}
{% set mayPlan = door('roster.record', area) %}

{% block title %}{{ area.name }} · Roster · week{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Roster{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}People down, days across &middot; fill from a pattern or by hand{% endblock %}

{% block roster_trail_tail %} <a href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::OVERVIEW_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">roster</a> / week{% endblock %}

{# THE PAGE'S OWN ACTION, IN THE TOP HEADER and never floating in the body.
   ONLY "Plan the day" is written here: the frame appends Configure to every
   tab of a module that has configuration sections, so a second one typed
   here renders the design's two-button row as three. #}
{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {% if mayPlan %}
        <a class="cta" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::PLAN_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid, day: window.today.format('Y-m-d')}) }}">{{ ux_icon('roster:pencil') }} Plan the day</a>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block roster_page %}
    {% set here = constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::WEEK_ROUTE') %}
    {% set base = {uuid: area.uuid, weeks: window.weeks} %}
    {% if chosenStation %}{% set base = base|merge({station: chosenStation.uuidString}) %}{% endif %}

    {# THE FOUR FIGURES, every one measuring the window the sheet under them
       draws — a band that counted a different fortnight would be a band
       nobody could check against the picture. #}
    <div class="factband">
        <span class="f"><span class="k">Rangers</span><span class="v">{{ sheet.rangers }}<em>across {{ sheet.stations }} station{{ sheet.stations == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</em></span></span>
        <span class="f"><span class="k">Days planned</span><span class="v">{{ sheet.daysPlanned }}<em>{{ window.weeks == 1 ? 'this week' : (window.weeks == 2 ? 'this fortnight' : 'these four weeks') }}{% if sheet.filledTo %} &middot; filled to {{ sheet.filledTo|date('j M')|lower }}{% endif %}</em></span></span>
        <span class="f"><span class="k">Short cover</span><span class="v">{{ sheet.shortCover }}<em>station-days under the number</em></span></span>
        <span class="f"><span class="k">Edited by hand</span><span class="v">{{ sheet.editedByHand }}<em>a pattern will not touch them</em></span></span>
        <span class="sp"></span>
        <a class="more" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SETTINGS_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Roster settings &rarr;</a>
    </div>

    {# ====================================================================
       THE FILL ROW — the only thing above the sheet card (layout C). A
       pattern, a station, a start date, and the two buttons; and under it,
       in words, what the fill would do and what it obeys.
       ==================================================================== #}
    {% if mayPlan and stations is not empty and fillPatterns is not empty %}
        <form class="prow" method="post" data-controller="roster--fill"
              action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::SHEET_FILL_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="weeks" value="{{ window.weeks }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ window.from.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-roster--fill-target="window">

            <span class="k">Fill from a pattern</span>

            <select class="fld" name="station" aria-label="Which station">
                {% for station in stations %}
                    <option value="{{ station.uuidString }}" {{ chosenStation and chosenStation.id == station.id ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ station.name }}{% if station.code %} &middot; {{ station.code }}{% endif %}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>

            {# THE CHOSEN CYCLE, DRAWN. The strip is redrawn from the select's
               own data rather than fetched: the cycles are already on the
               page, and a round trip to colour five squares would be one. #}
            <span class="pstrip lg" data-roster--fill-target="strip"
                  data-colours="{{ patternColours|json_encode }}"></span>

            <select class="fld" name="pattern" aria-label="Which pattern" data-roster--fill-target="pattern"
                    data-action="roster--fill#redraw">
                {% for pattern in fillPatterns %}
                    <option value="{{ pattern.uuid }}" data-cycle="{{ pattern.cycle|json_encode }}">{{ pattern.name }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>

            <span class="k">from</span>
            <select class="fld" name="from" aria-label="Starting when">
                {% for start in startDates %}
                    <option value="{{ start.format('Y-m-d') }}" {{ start == window.from ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ start.format('D j M')|lower }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>

            {# PREVIEW AND FILL ARE ONE THING AND WRAP AS ONE: a flex line
               wraps before it shrinks, and a loose "Fill these days" was
               dropping alone onto a second row. #}
            <span class="pact">
                <button type="submit" class="btn sm" name="preview" value="1">Preview</button>
                <button type="submit" class="cta">Fill these days</button>
            </span>
        </form>

        {# WHAT A FILL OBEYS, STATED AND NOT EDITED. RULED 21 sep: the rules
           moved to the Watches card, so this is a caption and nothing in it
           is clickable but the door. #}
        <div class="prow2">
            {%- if fillPreview -%}
                Would fill <b>{{ fillPreview.days }} day{{ fillPreview.days == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</b> to <time datetime="{{ fillPreview.through.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ fillPreview.through.format('D j M')|lower }}</time> &middot; leaves <b>{{ fillPreview.leftAlone }} edited day{{ fillPreview.leftAlone == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</b> as {{ fillPreview.leftAlone == 1 ? 'it is' : 'they are' }} &middot; a later start date changes only the days after it
            {%- else -%}
                Fills forward only &middot; a later start date changes only the days after it
            {%- endif -%}
            <span class="pfills">fills <b>{{ fillRules.ahead }}</b> ahead &middot; <b>{{ fillRules.rest }}</b> rest &middot; {{ fillRules.nightThenDay }} &middot; <a href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Watches &rarr;</a></span>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# ====================================================================
       THE SHEET. A bounded card whose HEAD carries every control it has and
       whose BODY is the only thing that scrolls.
       ==================================================================== #}
    <div class="c rband sheetcard" data-controller="roster--sheet roster--sheet-folds roster--day-menu"
         data-roster--sheet-folds-url-value="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::SHEET_PREFS_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}"
         data-roster--sheet-folds-token-value="{{ csrfToken }}">
        <div class="rb-hd shead">
            <span class="tab">The sheet</span>
            <span class="rb-ttl">{{ sheet.rangers }} ranger{{ sheet.rangers == 1 ? '' : 's' }} across {{ sheet.stations }} station{{ sheet.stations == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>

            {# THE CALENDAR TAB'S OWN NAV, and it is the calendar's markup:
               the window is the one `on` chip and everything that acts is a
               ghost chip. #}
            <span class="shnav">
                <a class="mchip ghost" href="{{ path(here, base|merge({from: window.previous.format('Y-m-d')})) }}" aria-label="The weeks before">&lsaquo;</a>
                <span class="mchip on">{{ window.label }}</span>
                <a class="mchip ghost" href="{{ path(here, base|merge({from: window.next.format('Y-m-d')})) }}" aria-label="The weeks after">&rsaquo;</a>
                <a class="mchip ghost" href="{{ path(here, base) }}">Today</a>
            </span>

            <span class="shsp"></span>

            {# THE HOUSE'S GROUPED DROPDOWN, which is a `<details>`: it opens,
               chooses and clears with no script of ours, and a filtered
               sheet is a url somebody can send. #}
            <details class="i-dd">
                <summary class="mchip i-ddt">
                    <span class="i-ddval">{{ chosenStation ? (chosenStation.name|lower ~ (chosenStation.code ? ' · ' ~ chosenStation.code|lower : '')) : 'all stations · ' ~ sheet.stations }}</span><span class="i-ddcaret">&#9662;</span>
                </summary>
                <div class="i-ddmenu" aria-label="station">
                    <span class="i-ddhead">station</span>
                    <a class="i-ddopt{{ chosenStation ? '' : ' on' }}" href="{{ path(here, {uuid: area.uuid, weeks: window.weeks, from: window.from.format('Y-m-d')}) }}"><span class="i-dot"></span><span class="i-ddopt-l">All stations with somebody stationed</span><span class="i-ddopt-n">{{ sheet.stations }}</span></a>
                    <span class="i-ddsep"></span>
                    {% for option in stationOptions %}
                        <a class="i-ddopt{{ chosenStation and chosenStation.uuidString == option.uuid ? ' on' : '' }}"
                           href="{{ path(here, {uuid: area.uuid, weeks: window.weeks, from: window.from.format('Y-m-d'), station: option.uuid}) }}"><span class="i-dot"></span><span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ option.name }}{% if option.code %} &middot; {{ option.code }}{% endif %}</span><span class="i-ddopt-n">{{ option.rangers }}</span></a>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </details>

            {# ONE, TWO OR FOUR, and never anything between: anything between
               a week and a month is a stretched fortnight. Four is the MONTH
               view and compacts the cell the way the calendar does. #}
            <details class="i-dd">
                <summary class="mchip i-ddt">
                    <span class="i-ddval">{{ {1: 'one week', 2: 'two weeks', 4: 'four weeks'}[window.weeks] }}</span><span class="i-ddcaret">&#9662;</span>
                </summary>
                <div class="i-ddmenu" aria-label="weeks in view">
                    <span class="i-ddhead">weeks in view</span>
                    {% for weeks, label in {1: 'One week', 2: 'Two weeks', 4: 'Four weeks'} %}
                        <a class="i-ddopt{{ window.weeks == weeks ? ' on' : '' }}"
                           href="{{ path(here, base|merge({weeks: weeks, from: window.from.format('Y-m-d')})) }}"><span class="i-dot"></span><span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ label }}</span>
                            {%- if weeks == 2 %}<span class="i-ddopt-n">the default</span>{% elseif weeks == 4 %}<span class="i-ddopt-n">a month, cells compacted</span>{% endif -%}
                        </a>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </details>

            <button type="button" class="mchip ghost" data-action="roster--sheet-folds#foldAll">Fold all</button>
            <button type="button" class="mchip ghost" data-action="roster--sheet-folds#openAll">Open all</button>
        </div>

        <div class="rb-body">
            {% if sheet.isEmpty %}
                <div class="rfrag"><b>No station is on the area&rsquo;s books</b><em>a sheet is people down at a place, so the first station comes first</em></div>
            {% else %}
                <div class="psheetwrap {{ window.widthClass }}" data-roster--sheet-target="scroller">
                    <table class="fg-rota csheet">
                        <colgroup><col class="who">{% for day in days %}<col class="dy">{% endfor %}</colgroup>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th class="who">Ranger</th>
                                {% for day in days %}
                                    <th class="{{ day == window.today ? 'today' : '' }}"{{ day == window.today ? ' data-roster--sheet-target="today"' : '' }}>
                                        <time datetime="{{ day.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ day.format('D')|lower }}<em>{{ day.format('j') }}</em></time>
                                    </th>
                                {% endfor %}
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            {% for band in sheet.bands %}
                                {% set shut = band.foldKey in folded %}
                                {# A FOLD HEAD IS A ROW and not a `<details>`: a
                                   `<details>` cannot wrap `<tr>`s, and the day
                                   columns have to stay in one grid across every
                                   station. Same chevron, same head line. #}
                                <tr class="stfold {{ shut ? 'shut' : 'open' }}" data-fold="{{ band.foldKey }}">
                                    {# THE HEAD'S LEADING CELL IS ONE COLUMN WIDE, so the
                                       station reads down two lines instead of across a
                                       merged band: the name and the fold, then the code,
                                       how many are stationed there, and how many days it
                                       stands short. #}
                                    <td class="sep">
                                        <button type="button" class="stfoldb" aria-expanded="{{ shut ? 'false' : 'true' }}"
                                                data-action="roster--sheet-folds#toggle">
                                            <span class="stline">
                                                {{ ux_icon('roster:chevron-down', {class: 'pmf-car', width: 12, height: 12}) }}
                                                <b>{{ band.stationName }}</b>
                                            </span>
                                            {# A FOLDED STATION STILL STATES HOW MANY DAYS
                                               IT IS SHORT, in the alarm ink: folding is for
                                               length and may never hide a gap. #}
                                            <span class="stmeta">
                                                {%- if band.stationCode %}<span class="mono">{{ band.stationCode }}</span> &middot; {% endif -%}
                                                {%- if band.rangers -%}
                                                    {{ band.rangers }} ranger{{ band.rangers == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                                                    {%- if band.shortDays %} &middot; <span class="sh">{{ band.shortDays }} short this window</span>{% endif -%}
                                                {%- else -%}
                                                    <span class="ok">nobody stationed here</span>
                                                {%- endif -%}
                                            </span>
                                        </button>
                                    </td>

                                    {# AND ONE COVER TOKEN UNDER EVERY DAY COLUMN. A GAP
                                       BELONGS TO THE STATION, NOT TO A RANGER: what is
                                       short is this place on this day, against the number
                                       this place says it needs. A station that names no
                                       number counts its planned rangers against the rangers
                                       stationed there, and is never short — nothing asked
                                       is not a failure. #}
                                    {% for day in band.cover %}
                                        <td class="sepd{{ day.isToday ? ' today' : '' }}"><span class="cvr {{ day.state.className }}">{{ day.label }}</span></td>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </tr>

                                {% for row in band.rows %}
                                    <tr class="strow" data-of="{{ band.foldKey }}" {{ shut ? 'hidden' : '' }}>
                                        <td class="who"><b>{{ row.personName }}</b>{% if row.stationCode %}<em>{{ row.stationCode }}</em>{% endif %}</td>
                                        {% for cell in row.cells %}
                                            <td class="{{ cell.isToday ? 'today' : '' }}">
                                                {{ include('@UhifadhiRoster/week/_cell.html.twig', {
                                                    area: area, cell: cell, row: row, band: band, window: window,
                                                    mayPlan: mayPlan, csrfToken: csrfToken, shifts: shifts,
                                                }, with_context: false) }}
                                            </td>
                                        {% endfor %}
                                    </tr>
                                {% endfor %}
                            {% endfor %}
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                {# THE KEY. The area's own shifts in the area's own colours, so
                   nobody is ever asked what a tint means. #}
                <div class="pkey">
                    {% for shift in shifts %}
                        <span><i class="k" data-cat="{{ shift.colour }}"></i>{{ shift.label|lower }}</span>
                    {% endfor %}
                    <span><i class="k o"></i>off &mdash; nothing drawn</span>
                    <span><i class="k h"></i>edited by hand</span>
                    <span class="sp"></span>
                    <span>{{ sheet.shortCover }} short station-day{{ sheet.shortCover == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot; {{ sheet.editedByHand }} edited by hand &middot; {{ sheet.rangers }} ranger{{ sheet.rangers == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot; {{ window.label }}</span>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="height:12px"></div>

    {# ====================================================================
       THE SWAP IN PROGRESS. Two house cards: a trade states the two cells
       and what they cost, and a register shows every state an offer can end
       in. A swap is offered to the handset and accepted there, so the web
       app never puts a person on a watch they have not seen.
       ==================================================================== #}
    {# ONE COLUMN, the design's: the trade above, the register under it, each the full width — two cards side by side halved the rows a trade states. #}
    <h2 class="zone">The swap in progress</h2>
    <div class="grid">

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Swap a watch<span class="src">&middot; two cells, and what the trade costs</span></span>

            {% if offering %}
                <div class="rln"><span class="fog">Give up</span><span><b>{{ offering.duty.person.fullName }}</b> <span class="mono">{{ offering.duty.onDay.format('D j')|lower }} &middot; {{ offering.duty.station.name }} {{ offering.duty.shiftKey }}</span></span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span class="fog">Take it</span><span><b>{{ offering.taking.fullName }}</b> <span class="chip acc">picked</span></span></div>

                {% for check in cost.checks %}
                    <div class="rln"><span class="fog">{{ check.label }}</span><span class="mono {{ check.holds ? 'g' : 'w' }}">{{ check.detail }}</span></div>
                {% endfor %}

                {% if mayPlan %}
                    <form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::OFFER_SWAP_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="duty" value="{{ offering.duty.uuid }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="taking" value="{{ offering.taking.uuidString }}">
                        <div class="staddrow"><span class="sp"></span>
                            <a class="btn sm" href="{{ path(here, base) }}">Cancel</a>
                            <button type="submit" class="cta">Send the offer</button>
                        </div>
                    </form>
                {% endif %}
            {% else %}
                <div class="rln"><span class="fog">Give up</span><span class="fog">pick a day from the sheet above</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span class="fog">Take it</span><span class="fog">then the person to ask</span></div>
                <div class="rfrag"><b>An offer moves nobody</b><em>until the handset accepts, both watches stand exactly as they were filled</em></div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Swaps<span class="src">&middot; this window &middot; latest {{ recent|length }}</span></span>

            {% for swap in recent %}
                <div class="rln">
                    {#- THE STATION BY ITS CODE, and after the chip the design's phrase for
                        the state. An offer's sent time is the instant its identifier was
                        minted — a v7 uuid carries it, so no column says it twice. -#}
                    <span><b>{{ swap.offeredTo.fullName }}</b> <span class="mono">
                        {{- swap.state.value == 'accepted' ? 'took' : (swap.state.value == 'offered' ? 'takes' : 'asked for') }}
                        {{ swap.duty.person.fullName }}&rsquo;s {{ swap.duty.onDay.format('D j')|lower }} {{ swap.duty.shiftKey }} at {{ swap.duty.station.code }}</span></span>
                    <span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px">
                        <span class="chip {{ {'offered': 'acc', 'accepted': 'ok', 'declined': 'fail', 'withdrawn': 'idle'}[swap.state.value] }}">{{ swap.state.label }}</span>
                        <span class="mono d">
                            {%- if swap.state.value == 'offered' -%}
                                sent <time datetime="{{ swap.uuid.dateTime.format('c') }}" data-localtime-format="time">{{ swap.uuid.dateTime.format('H:i') }}</time>, not answered
                            {%- elseif swap.state.value == 'accepted' -%}
                                accepted on the handset {% if swap.respondedAt %}<time datetime="{{ swap.respondedAt.format('c') }}" data-localtime-format="time">{{ swap.respondedAt.format('H:i') }}</time>{% endif %}
                            {%- elseif swap.state.value == 'declined' -%}
                                declined {% if swap.respondedAt %}<time datetime="{{ swap.respondedAt.format('c') }}" data-localtime-format="time">{{ swap.respondedAt.format('H:i') }}</time>{% endif %} &mdash; {{ swap.note ?: 'no reason given' }}
                            {%- else -%}
                                withdrawn by {{ swap.offeredBy ? swap.offeredBy.fullName : 'the duty officer' }}
                            {%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% else %}
                <div class="rfrag"><b>No swap in this window</b><em>every watch is standing exactly as it was filled</em></div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

    </div>
{% endblock %}
